{"id":"e6e7e582-c648-4561-a2e6-1b5368252389","object":"chat.completion","created":1785016701,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case['segments']\\n    budget = case['budget']\\n    n = len(segments)\\n    mins = [s['minimum'] for s in segments]\\n    caps = [s['capacity'] for s in segments]\\n    importance = [s['importance'] for s in segments]\\n    \\n    # validate budget\\n    sum_mins = sum(mins)\\n    sum_caps = sum(caps)\\n    if budget < sum_mins or budget > sum_caps:\\n        # fallback: allocate minimum only, ignore budget? But spec says reject,\\n        # so we raise an error to ensure the caller sees invalid input.\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Invalid budget: below sum of minima or above total capacity\\\")\\n    \\n    alloc = list(mins)  # initialize at minimum\\n    remaining = budget - sum_mins\\n    \\n    while remaining > 0:\\n        best_score = -1.0\\n        best_idx = -1\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            if alloc[i] >= caps[i]:\\n                continue\\n            # score = importance / (next position)\\n            score = importance[i] / (alloc[i] + 1)\\n            if score > best_score:\\n                best_score = score\\n                best_idx = i\\n            # tie: keep earlier (original order) -> since we iterate in order,\\n            # only update if strictly greater\\n        # allocate one token to best_idx\\n        alloc[best_idx] += 1\\n        remaining -= 1\\n    \\n    by_name = {}\\n    for i, seg in enumerate(segments):\\n        by_name[seg['name']] = alloc[i]\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'allocations': alloc,\\n        'by_name': by_name,\\n        'total': budget\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python implementation of `solve(case)` that matches the schema. The problem: allocate budget tokens to segments with given importance, minimum, capacity. Initia